From: Dalton Alexandre <alley.nightly_0b@icloud.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 15:49:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: soc: apple: Add the T8010 Always-On Processor

The Always-On Processor (AOP) of the A10 is an ARMv7 coprocessor running
RTKit firmware for the motion sensors and the always-on microphones. Its
firmware is board-specific and loaded by the operating system: a main
image into the AOP's SRAM and an external segment into system memory.
It talks to the application processor through an A7 IOP mailbox.

The bootloader fills in the chip's ECID, which the firmware's boot
arguments carry.

[Orchard: from dl-alexandre/orchard db7f4e7 (orchard PR #36); reworked
 for an in-kernel driver: AKF control/boot control/SRAM regions, a
 separate mailbox node, firmware names and the ECID property.]
Signed-off-by: Dalton Alexandre <alley.nightly_0b@icloud.com>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../bindings/soc/apple/apple,t8010-aop.yaml   | 79 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 79 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/apple/apple,t8010-aop.yaml

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/apple/apple,t8010-aop.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/apple/apple,t8010-aop.yaml
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..73b7c5d51
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/apple/apple,t8010-aop.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,79 @@
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: (GPL-2.0-only OR BSD-2-Clause)
+%YAML 1.2
+---
+$id: http://devicetree.org/schemas/soc/apple/apple,t8010-aop.yaml#
+$schema: http://devicetree.org/meta-schemas/core.yaml#
+
+title: Apple T8010 Always-On Processor
+
+maintainers:
+  - Dalton Alexandre <alley.nightly_0b@icloud.com>
+
+description:
+  The Always-On Processor (AOP) of the A10 is an ARMv7 coprocessor that
+  runs RTKit firmware and serves the motion sensors (accelerometer,
+  gyroscope, compass, pressure) and the always-on microphones. It runs from
+  local SRAM, with a further firmware segment in system memory, and talks
+  to the application processor through an A7 IOP mailbox. Its firmware is
+  board-specific and is loaded by the operating system.
+
+properties:
+  compatible:
+    const: apple,t8010-aop
+
+  reg:
+    items:
+      - description: AKF coprocessor control registers
+      - description: Always-on boot control registers
+      - description: Local SRAM
+
+  reg-names:
+    items:
+      - const: akf
+      - const: control
+      - const: sram
+
+  mboxes:
+    maxItems: 1
+
+  mbox-names:
+    const: mbox
+
+  firmware-name:
+    items:
+      - description: Main image, loaded into the local SRAM
+      - description: External segment, loaded into system memory
+
+  apple,ecid:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint64
+    description:
+      The chip's unique ID (ECID), filled in by the bootloader. The
+      firmware's boot arguments carry it.
+
+required:
+  - compatible
+  - reg
+  - reg-names
+  - mboxes
+  - mbox-names
+  - firmware-name
+
+additionalProperties: false
+
+examples:
+  - |
+    soc {
+        #address-cells = <2>;
+        #size-cells = <2>;
+
+        aop@210800000 {
+            compatible = "apple,t8010-aop";
+            reg = <0x2 0x10800000 0x0 0x4000>,
+                  <0x2 0x10000500 0x0 0x100>,
+                  <0x2 0x10e00000 0x0 0xa0000>;
+            reg-names = "akf", "control", "sram";
+            mboxes = <&aop_mbox>;
+            mbox-names = "mbox";
+            firmware-name = "apple/aop-ipad7b.bin", "apple/aop-ipad7b-ext.bin";
+        };
+    };
